  --api-key <key>       API key (or set TINES_API_KEY, or run \`tines login\`)
  --json                output the raw JSON response
  -h, --help            display help for command
",
  "tines issues": "Usage: tines issues [options] [command]

Work with issues

Options:
  -h, --help                                            display help for command

Commands:
  list [options]                                        List issues across projects (hides done issues unless --all)
  create [options] <project>                            Create an issue in a project, optionally with a recurrence (a scheduled task)
  show [options] <ref>                                  Show an issue (<project>/<number>), including allowed transitions
  edit [options] <ref>                                  Edit an issue: title, description, workflow, or force-set state
  move [options] <ref> <action>                         Take a transition on an issue by its action name (e.g. "approve")
  comment [options] <ref> <markdown>                    Comment on an issue — Markdown body: inline text, @file, or "-" to read stdin; escape a literal leading @ as @@
  comment-edit [options] <ref> <comment-id> <markdown>  Replace the body of your own comment — Markdown body: inline text, @file, or "-" to read stdin; escape a literal leading @ as @@
  comment-delete [options] <ref> <comment-id>           Delete your own comment (the event keeps the record of the deletion)
  label [options] <ref> <name...>                       Add labels to an issue (a label that does not exist yet is created)
  unlabel [options] <ref> <name...>                     Remove labels from an issue
  block [options] <blocker> <blocked>                   Record that <blocker> blocks <blocked> (advisory: transitions stay allowed)
  unblock [options] <blocker> <blocked>                 Remove the link making <blocker> block <blocked>
  duplicate|dupe [options] <ref> <canonical>            Mark <ref> as a duplicate of <canonical> (its state then follows <canonical>)
  context [options] <ref>                               Print an issue's effective context (the assembled bundle for its current state)
  unduplicate|undupe [options] <ref>                    Unmark a duplicate (its own state was never changed, so it simply reappears)
  prompt [options] <ref>                                Print the launch prompt: the stitched context followed by the issue block
  artifacts                                             Typed, versioned attachments on an issue — the work products transition requirements gate on
  assign [options] <ref> [runner]                       Pin an issue to a runner (<runner>[:tier]) — replaces routing rules for it; --clear unpins
  dispatch [options] <ref>                              Explain why an issue is (not) dispatching: eligibility, routing, per-runner verdicts
  resume [options] <ref>                                Un-park an issue: clear needs-attention and reset the attempt count
  help [command]                                        display help for command
",
  "tines issues artifacts": "Usage: tines issues artifacts [options] [command]

Typed, versioned attachments on an issue — the work products transition
requirements gate on

Options:
  -h, --help                              display help for command

Commands:
  list [options] <ref>                    List the artifacts attached to an issue
  show [options] <ref> <name>             Show an artifact with its full version history
  attach [options] <ref> <name> [source]  Attach content to a named artifact slot (creates it, or appends the next version)
  reaffirm [options] <ref> <name>         Bless the current content as fresh (appends a version reusing the same payload)
  get [options] <ref> <name>              Fetch content (current version by default); a link/pr prints its URL
  delete [options] <ref> <name>           Delete an artifact — every version and its stored files (history is not recoverable)
  help [command]                          display help for command
",
  "tines issues artifacts attach": "Usage: tines issues artifacts attach [options] <ref> <name> [source]

Attach content to a named artifact slot (creates it, or appends the next
version)

Options:
  -f, --file <path>         upload a file (MIME sniffed from the extension)
  --folder <dir>            snapshot a directory tree as one version (collect
                            locally, attach once; MIME per file sniffed)
  -t, --text <md|@file>     inline text document: inline Markdown or @file
  --link <url>              link: the URL to attach
  --pr <spec>               PR reference: owner/repo#N or a GitHub PR URL
  --content-type <mime>     declared MIME type (with --file or --text)
  --filename <name>         display filename (with --text; defaults to
                            <name>.md)
  --title <title>           display title (with --link)
  -d, --description <text>  artifact description, shown in lists and launch
                            prompts
  --ignore-gates            attach this type even when a transition requirement
                            rejects it (skips inference and the pre-flight
                            checks)
  -u, --url <url>           base URL of the Tines API (or set TINES_API_URL, or
                            run \`tines login\`; default
                            https://tines.tbuckley.dev)
  --api-key <key>           API key (or set TINES_API_KEY, or run \`tines login\`)
  --json                    output the raw JSON response
  -h, --help                display help for command
