  "tines issues create": "Usage: tines issues create [options] <project>

Create an issue in a project, optionally with a recurrence (a scheduled task)

Options:
  -t, --title <title>           issue title (doubles as the title template with
                                a recurrence)
  -d, --description <markdown>  issue description (Markdown) — inline text,
                                @file, or "-" to read stdin; escape a literal
                                leading @ as @@
  -w, --workflow <id-or-name>   workflow (defaults to project default, else
                                standard)
  -s, --state <name>            starting state (defaults to the workflow's
                                initial state)
  --every <preset>              repeat hourly (or every N hours: "6h"), daily,
                                weekly, or monthly
  --at <when>                   preset time of day HH:MM (default 09:00); for
                                hourly, the minute past the hour :MM (default
                                :00)
  --on <when>                   weekday (weekly) or day of month (monthly)
  --cron <expr>                 5-field cron expression (alternative to
                                --every/--at/--on)
  --tz <iana>                   schedule timezone (defaults to the system
                                timezone)
  --if-closed                   only create a new instance when all previous
                                instances are closed
  --schedule-name <name>        schedule name, unique per project (defaults to
                                the title)
  -l, --label <name>            attach a label; repeat for several (created if
                                new) (default: [])
  -u, --url <url>               base URL of the Tines API (or set TINES_API_URL,
                                or run \`tines login\`; default
                                https://tines.tbuckley.dev)
  --api-key <key>               API key (or set TINES_API_KEY, or run \`tines
