  -r, --runner <name>  filter by runner name
  --active             only runs holding a claim (assigned/launching/running)
  --limit <n>          maximum items to return (page size under --all-pages)
  --cursor <cursor>    resume from the next_cursor of a previous page
  --all-pages          fetch every page, not just the first (slower on large
                       lists)
  -u, --url <url>      base URL of the Tines API (or set TINES_API_URL, or run
                       \`tines login\`; default https://tines.tbuckley.dev)
  --api-key <key>      API key (or set TINES_API_KEY, or run \`tines login\`)
  --json               output the raw JSON response
  -h, --help           display help for command
",
  "tines runs show": "Usage: tines runs show [options] <id>

Show a run; --logs prints the captured log tail, --logs --full the whole log

Options:
  --logs           print the log tail
  --full           with --logs: print the complete log, not the 256 KB tail
  --raw            with --logs --full: print the unrendered harness stream
                   instead
  -u, --url <url>  base URL of the Tines API (or set TINES_API_URL, or run
                   \`tines login\`; default https://tines.tbuckley.dev)
  --api-key <key>  API key (or set TINES_API_KEY, or run \`tines login\`)
  --json           output the raw JSON response
  -h, --help       display help for command
",
  "tines schedules": "Usage: tines schedules [options] [command]

Manage scheduled tasks (addressed as <project>/<name>)

Options:
  -h, --help              display help for command

Commands:
  list [options]          List scheduled tasks (hides paused schedules unless
                          --all)
  show [options] <ref>    Show a schedule (<project>/<name>): config, next/last
                          run, recent instances
  edit [options] <ref>    Edit a schedule: templates, workflow, start state,
                          recurrence, timezone, gate, or name
  pause [options] <ref>   Pause a schedule (keeps config and history)
  resume [options] <ref>  Resume a paused schedule (recomputes the next
                          occurrence from now)
  run [options] <ref>     Create an instance now (respects the only-when-closed
                          gate)
  delete [options] <ref>  Delete a schedule (existing issues are kept)
  help [command]          display help for command
",
  "tines schedules delete": "Usage: tines schedules delete [options] <ref>

Delete a schedule (existing issues are kept)

Options:
  -y, --yes        skip the confirmation prompt
  -u, --url <url>  base URL of the Tines API (or set TINES_API_URL, or run
                   \`tines login\`; default https://tines.tbuckley.dev)
  --api-key <key>  API key (or set TINES_API_KEY, or run \`tines login\`)
  --json           output the raw JSON response
  -h, --help       display help for command
",
  "tines schedules edit": "Usage: tines schedules edit [options] <ref>

Edit a schedule: templates, workflow, start state, recurrence, timezone, gate,
or name

Options:
  -t, --title <template>        set the title template
  -d, --description <markdown>  set the description template (Markdown) — inline
                                text, @file, or "-" to read stdin; escape a
                                literal leading @ as @@
  -w, --workflow <id-or-name>   move future instances onto another workflow
                                (resets the start state to its initial state
                                unless --state is also given)
  -s, --state <id-or-name>      start state for future instances (the workflow's
                                initial state = the default)
  --every <preset>              repeat hourly (or every N hours: "6h"), daily,
                                weekly, or monthly
  --at <when>                   preset time of day HH:MM (default 09:00); for
                                hourly, the minute past the hour :MM (default
                                :00)
  --on <when>                   weekday (weekly) or day of month (monthly)
  --cron <expr>                 5-field cron expression (alternative to
                                --every/--at/--on)
  --tz <iana>                   set the schedule timezone
  --if-closed                   only create a new instance when all previous
                                instances are closed
  --no-if-closed                clear the only-when-closed gate
  --name <new-name>             rename the schedule
  -u, --url <url>               base URL of the Tines API (or set TINES_API_URL,
                                or run \`tines login\`; default
                                https://tines.tbuckley.dev)
  --api-key <key>               API key (or set TINES_API_KEY, or run \`tines
                                login\`)
  --json                        output the raw JSON response
  -h, --help                    display help for command
",
  "tines schedules list": "Usage: tines schedules list [options]

